  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 417c175362a0ec543944003b60e08110, type: 3}
  m_Name: OrderTuning_Balanced
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::ZoomZoom.Orders.OrderTuning
  profileName: Balanced
whyThisSetup: '50 s, set for the Milestone 1 build on 23 September. The countdown
    in Order begins at spawn and not at pickup, so the drive to the pickup is inside
    the same budget and is costed with the job. Across the 36 pairs formed by the
    twelve hand-placed delivery points, the shortest job is 260 m of grid driving
    including the approach, the mean is 557 m and the longest is 954 m, from the
    North East Corner to the South West Yard. Measured top speed is 32 m/s but cannot
    be held through junctions on the measured sideways grip of 13 m/s2, so jobs are
    costed at a 20 m/s working average: 13 s for the shortest, 28 s for the mean,
    48 s for the longest. 50 s clears all 36 pairs at that average, with about 2 s
    spare on the longest, so a player who drives the worst job cleanly makes it and
    one who takes a wrong turn on it does not. 45 s, the previous value, left that
    one pair about 3 s short. The 20 m/s average is an estimate from measured grip
    rather than a recorded lap; if real laps come in slower, move a drop-off before
    loosening the limit for every job. Run docs/tooling/scene-tools/order_distances.py
    50 to re-check after any change to the points or the limit.'
  spawnInterval: 12
  maxActiveOrders: 3
  orderTimeLimit: 50
  baseDeliveryValue: 10
  latePenaltyPerSecond: 1
  enableMultiLegOrders: 1
  multiLegChance: 0.5
  minTransferLegs: 1
  maxTransferLegs: 2
  extraTimePerTransferLeg: 15
